\pard \fs24\tx-720\tx0\tx612\tx1152\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8532\tx9072\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs36 \i\f2\fs36 Concerning the Service}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 Holy Baptism is full initiation by water and the Holy Spirit into\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 Christ's Body the Church.  The bond which God establishes in Baptism\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 is indissoluble.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 Holy Baptism is appropriately administered within the Eucharist as the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 chief service on a Sunday or other feast.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 The bishop, when present, is the celebrant; and is expected to preach the \softline
Word and preside at Baptism and the Eucharist.  At Baptism, the bishop \softline
officiates at the Presentation and Examination of the Candidates;\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 says the Thanksgiving over the Water; [consecrates the Chrism;] reads the \softline
prayer, "Heavenly Father, we thank you that by water and the Holy\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 Spirit;" and officiates at what follows.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 In the absence of a bishop, a priest is the celebrant and presides at the \softline
service.  If a priest uses Chrism in signing the newly baptized, it must have \softline
been previously consecrated by the bishop.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 Each candidate for Holy Baptism is to be sponsored by one or more\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 baptized persons.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 Sponsors of adults and older children present their candidates and\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 thereby signify their endorsement of the candidates and their intention to \softline
support them by prayer and example in their Christian life.  Sponsors of \softline
infants, commonly called godparents, present their candidates, make\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 promises in their own names, and also take vows on behalf of their\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 candidates.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 It is fitting that parents be included among the godparents of their own \softline
children.  Parents and godparents are to be instructed in the meaning of \softline
Baptism, in their duties to help the new Christians grow in the knowledge \softline
and love of God, and in their responsibilities as members of his Church.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 Additional Directions are on page 312.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 \par
